> Figure ES8: 16 enablers that break the four implementation barriers to accelerate action.
> Country experience shows this is achievable, not
> aspirational. At the institutional level, China’s co-control
> strategy for air pollution and climate change, Mexico’s
> Intersecretarial Commission on Climate Change, and
> Nigeria’s integration of short-lived climate pollutants
> into its Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC)
> illustrate how policy frameworks can be designed to
> strengthen cross-sectoral implementation.
> At the programme level, China’s expansion of electric
> vehicle charging infrastructure, India’s clean cooking
> access programme and solar mission, Mexico’s
> national cookstove projects and national strategy
> for electric mobility and Nigeria’s awareness-raising
> initiative on open burning and its Rural Women
> Energy Security programme show that well-designed
> interventions can drive social as well as technological
> change.
